---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout title="Caching — WhisperQueue">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-medium">Caching</h1>

  <p class="mt-4 text-wq-muted">
    WhisperQueue uses S3/MinIO ETag headers (MD5 of file content) as cache keys.
    A HEAD request checks the ETag before any download — no bandwidth wasted on cache hits.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-wq-border bg-wq-raised p-5 font-mono text-sm leading-8">
    POST /transcribe (s3://bucket/file.mp3)<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&darr;<br />
    HEAD request &rarr; get ETag (no download)<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&darr;<br />
    Check SQLite for existing transcript with that hash<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&darr; hit&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&darr; miss<br />
    Return transcript_id&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Download file<br />
    instantly, no job&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Queue job<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Process with faster-whisper<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Store result in SQLite<br />
    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Return transcript_id via /status
  </div>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">HTTPS URLs</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-wq-muted">
      For HTTPS URLs, WhisperQueue checks ETag or Content-MD5 response headers.
      If neither is present, it hashes the bytes during the single download pass — never downloads twice.
      Cache is checked after hashing; hits discard the temp file, misses proceed to transcription.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Multipart upload caveat</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-wq-muted">
      S3 multipart uploads produce a composite ETag (hash of hashes, not plain MD5).
      Rare for audio files but worth knowing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Bypassing the cache</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-wq-muted">
      Pass <code class="text-wq-accent-lt">?force=true</code> on <code class="text-wq-accent-lt">POST /transcribe</code> to re-transcribe
      a file that already has a cached result.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>